# .gitignore — dsh-link-start
#
# The first commit is SOURCE ONLY: every tracked path must be something a
# reader can build from, not something an install or a script produces.
# Everything excluded below is either a dependency install, a throwaway
# extraction, or regenerable output.
#
# READ THE LAST SECTION BEFORE ADDING A PATTERN. `lib/client.js` is a
# committed build artifact, and the obvious globs would drop it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# npm/pnpm install output. In this checkout it holds only an @deepseek-ai
# link (the schemastery/cosmokit peer), ~139 KB. Never source, never committed;
# a clone recreates it from package.json.
node_modules/

# No lockfile is committed. The single peer dependency is declared as `*`
# (INTERFACES.md §3) because DSH resolves it against the runtime's own copy, so a
# lockfile would pin nothing meaningful. Install is by directory junction, not by
# a package manager; `npm install` exists only to satisfy that one peer for the
# offline suites.
package-lock.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch: a third-party reference extraction
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ~23 MB of unpacked DSH reference source, kept only as a *shape* reference for
# docs and tooling (see AGENTS.md, "What it is"). It is a third-party
# extraction, not this package's source, and nothing here builds or verifies
# against it at runtime.
.scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated storyboard
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PNGs (one per phase), index.html and report.json — all written by
# `node tools/storyboard.mjs`, which walks `src/scene.js`'s frozen phase table
# and rasterises `frame(t)` through `tools/raster.mjs`. Fully regenerable, so a
# committed copy would be stale the moment the timeline changes. To review the
# animation, run the tool; do not commit its output.
storyboard/

# The verifier's scratch area: RED-BASELINE logs, tamper-test copies and other
# throwaway scaffolding produced while proving the gate is non-vacuous. Not
# source, not referenced by any suite.
verify/scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# lib/client.js is deliberately NOT ignored — do not add a pattern that catches it
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `lib/client.js` is a COMMITTED BUILD ARTIFACT (AGENTS.md; INTERFACES.md §3).
# The package manifest exports it as this plugin's browser bundle
# (`exports["./client"] -> ./lib/client.js`), and DSH's client-module graph
# serves that exact file. A clone without it has no settings card until someone
# runs `node build-client.mjs` — and nothing in DSH would say why.
#
# It is generated from `src/client.js` by `node build-client.mjs`: edit the
# source, rebuild, and commit BOTH. Never hand-edit the artifact.
#
# So: no `lib/`, no `lib/*.js`, no `*.js`, no `*.min.js`. A pattern like that
# would silently drop the bundle from the first public commit.
